WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.385
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:08.967
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:17.538
Unit sixty: Proficiency Champion!. In this unit, you will celebrate C2 mastery and adapt your voice to any audience.

4
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.166
mastery of nuance.

5
00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:26.546
mastery of nuance means the ability to express very fine differences in meaning.

6
00:00:26.846 --> 00:00:31.423
Your mastery of nuance lets you disagree politely and precisely.

7
00:00:32.123 --> 00:00:35.530
Your turn. Say: mastery of nuance.

8
00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.614
mastery of nuance.

9
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:42.094
stylistic range.

10
00:00:42.794 --> 00:00:47.789
stylistic range means the ability to write and speak in many different styles.

11
00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:51.888
Your stylistic range covers poems, reports and speeches.

12
00:00:52.588 --> 00:00:56.204
Your turn. Say: stylistic range.

13
00:00:58.904 --> 00:01:00.323
stylistic range.

14
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:03.142
native-like command.

15
00:01:03.842 --> 00:01:09.986
native-like command means control of a language comparable to a highly educated native speaker.

16
00:01:10.286 --> 00:01:14.840
C2 learners show native-like command of idiom and register.

17
00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.783
Your turn. Say: native-like command.

18
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:24.703
native-like command.

19
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:27.136
eloquent writing.

20
00:01:27.836 --> 00:01:32.366
eloquent writing means writing that is clear, graceful and persuasive.

21
00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:35.420
Eloquent writing can move readers to action.

22
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.446
Your turn. Say: eloquent writing.

23
00:01:42.146 --> 00:01:43.484
eloquent writing.

24
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:46.251
academic excellence.

25
00:01:46.951 --> 00:01:51.307
academic excellence means outstanding achievement in study and research.

26
00:01:51.607 --> 00:01:55.894
Academic excellence opens doors to universities worldwide.

27
00:01:56.594 --> 00:02:00.187
Your turn. Say: academic excellence.

28
00:02:02.887 --> 00:02:04.340
academic excellence.

29
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.943
intellectual maturity.

30
00:02:07.643 --> 00:02:13.323
intellectual maturity means the ability to think independently, fairly and deeply.

31
00:02:13.623 --> 00:02:17.852
Intellectual maturity means considering views you disagree with.

32
00:02:18.552 --> 00:02:22.028
Your turn. Say: intellectual maturity.

33
00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:26.356
intellectual maturity.

34
00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:28.769
lifelong scholar.

35
00:02:29.469 --> 00:02:33.942
lifelong scholar means a person who keeps studying and learning throughout life.

36
00:02:34.242 --> 00:02:37.866
A lifelong scholar is never finished with learning.

37
00:02:38.566 --> 00:02:42.206
Your turn. Say: lifelong scholar.

38
00:02:44.906 --> 00:02:46.429
lifelong scholar.

39
00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:49.056
C2 certificate.

40
00:02:49.756 --> 00:02:54.809
C2 certificate means an official document confirming the highest level of the CEFR.

41
00:02:55.109 --> 00:02:58.003
Rithy proudly received his C2 certificate.

42
00:02:58.703 --> 00:03:02.063
Your turn. Say: C2 certificate.

43
00:03:04.763 --> 00:03:06.252
C2 certificate.

44
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.760
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:15.267
Rithy, congratulations! You've completed sixty units of Online Proficiency.

46
00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:20.873
Thank you, Ms. Sarah. I never imagined I'd reach C2.

47
00:03:22.183 --> 00:03:27.239
Let's test your stylistic range. Describe your achievement to a university panel.

48
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:34.767
'Completion of this programme reflects sustained commitment and a native-like command of English.'

49
00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:38.830
Excellent. Now tell your little sister.

50
00:03:40.117 --> 00:03:44.388
'Guess what? I did it! I finished the top level of English!'

51
00:03:45.683 --> 00:03:48.614
Perfect style shifting. What will you do next?

52
00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:56.818
Keep learning. A C2 certificate is not the finish line; it's the starting line of a lifelong scholar.

53
00:03:58.117 --> 00:04:02.740
Grammar focus: Style shifting and audience (C2 review).

54
00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:06.073
At C2, you choose your voice for every audience.

55
00:04:06.373 --> 00:04:14.345
Formally: completion of this programme reflects sustained commitment. Informally: guess what? I did it!

56
00:04:14.645 --> 00:04:19.373
A C2 certificate is not the finish line; it's the starting line.

57
00:04:19.673 --> 00:04:26.003
True proficiency is not one perfect style but the freedom to choose the right voice for every listener.

58
00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:30.795
Now read and listen. The Journey from K0 to C2.

59
00:04:31.095 --> 00:04:34.082
Every journey to C2 begins with a single word.

60
00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:41.516
For many C2-EPE learners, that word was spoken years ago in a kindergarten class.

61
00:04:42.817 --> 00:04:51.376
Step by step, they moved through stories, songs, dialogues and debates, from simple sentences to complex arguments.

62
00:04:52.683 --> 00:05:00.604
At C2, learners demonstrate mastery of nuance, stylistic range and native-like command of the language.

63
00:05:01.917 --> 00:05:08.595
They can produce eloquent writing, analyse difficult texts and adapt their style to any audience.

64
00:05:09.883 --> 00:05:17.572
Yet proficiency is about more than academic excellence; it also reflects intellectual maturity and respect for others.

65
00:05:18.883 --> 00:05:25.097
A C2 certificate opens doors to universities, careers and international friendships.

66
00:05:26.383 --> 00:05:34.107
Above all, it marks the beginning of life as a lifelong scholar, curious, humble and ready to keep learning.

67
00:05:35.417 --> 00:05:38.115
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:38.415 --> 00:05:41.843
The ability to write and speak in many styles is blank.

69
00:05:42.143 --> 00:05:47.817
A, stylistic range. B, academic excellence. C, C2 certificate.

70
00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:54.675
The answer is A: stylistic range.

71
00:05:56.183 --> 00:05:59.123
Which sentence suits a university panel?

72
00:05:59.423 --> 00:06:07.236
A, Completion of this programme reflects sustained commitment.. B, Guess what? I did it!. C, Yay, finished!.

73
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:16.338
The answer is A: Completion of this programme reflects sustained commitment..

74
00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.268
Which sentence suits a little sister?

75
00:06:20.568 --> 00:06:28.566
A, Guess what? I did it!. B, This achievement constitutes a milestone.. C, Completion reflects commitment..

76
00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:36.154
The answer is A: Guess what? I did it!.

77
00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:40.706
A person who keeps learning throughout life is a blank.

78
00:06:41.006 --> 00:06:48.282
A, lifelong scholar. B, native-like command. C, mastery of nuance.

79
00:06:52.283 --> 00:06:55.119
The answer is A: lifelong scholar.

80
00:06:56.617 --> 00:07:00.439
According to the text, what does a C2 certificate mark?

81
00:07:00.739 --> 00:07:08.560
A, the beginning of life as a lifelong scholar. B, the end of learning. C, a final exam only.

82
00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:16.988
The answer is A: the beginning of life as a lifelong scholar.

83
00:07:18.483 --> 00:07:26.778
Now it's your turn. Part one: Look back on your English journey: what helped you most, and what will you do next?

84
00:07:32.078 --> 00:07:39.105
Part two: Answer twice: first formally for a scholarship panel, then informally for a friend.

85
00:07:45.405 --> 00:07:58.866
Formally: consistent practice and supportive teachers enabled me to achieve proficiency, and I intend to pursue further study abroad. Informally: honestly, the speaking practice changed everything, and now I want to keep going!

86
00:07:59.166 --> 00:08:01.212
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:08:02.217 --> 00:08:08.364
Great work today! You learned eight new words and style shifting and audience (c2 review).

88
00:08:08.664 --> 00:08:12.454
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

89
00:08:12.754 --> 00:08:21.016
Congratulations! You have completed the whole C2-EPE Online programme, from K0 to C2. We are so proud of you!

90
00:08:21.316 --> 00:08:23.760
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

